 "api_error_status": null,
 "result": "I couldn't get the customer name: the database has stayed locked through 15 tries in a row. That includes a bare `SELECT 1`, and plain reads from each table failed too. Since even the simplest query fails, another process is probably holding a lock on the database file. More retries from my side are unlikely to help until that lock is released, so I've stopped rather than keep using up your budget.\n\nThe query that will answer your question once the lock clears:\n\n```sql\nSELECT o.id, o.ordered_on, c.name\nFROM orders o JOIN customers c ON c.id = o.customer_id\nWHERE o.ordered_on < '2026-10-01'\nORDER BY o.ordered_on DESC\nLIMIT 1;\n```\n\nThis assumes `ordered_on` is stored as ISO text (`YYYY-MM-DD`). I couldn't check the actual format because nothing could be read. If dates are stored some other way, such as `DD/MM/YYYY`, comparing them as text will give the wrong answer.\n\nTo fix it, find and close whatever is holding the database open: an open SQLite shell, a write that's still running, or a stuck process. Then tell me and I'll run the query.",
